WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:16.018
Unit nine: B1 Preliminary: Listening. Today you will listen for gist, detail and opinions in four parts.

4
00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:18.912
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:22.856
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:24.428
Gist.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:27.056
Gist means the general meaning.

8
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.034
Listen for the gist.

9
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.768
Your turn. Say: Gist.

10
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:35.367
Gist.

11
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:37.095
Detail.

12
00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:41.070
Detail means a specific piece of information.

13
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:43.195
Listen for details.

14
00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:46.331
Your turn. Say: Detail.

15
00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.086
Detail.

16
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.584
Opinion.

17
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:54.594
Opinion means what someone thinks.

18
00:00:55.183 --> 00:00:56.428
What is her opinion?

19
00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:59.890
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

20
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:03.572
Opinion.

21
00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:05.167
Agree.

22
00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:08.415
Agree means to have the same opinion.

23
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:10.389
They agree on the date.

24
00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:13.473
Your turn. Say: Agree.

25
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:17.276
Agree.

26
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:19.087
Disagree.

27
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.245
Disagree means to have a different opinion.

28
00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.548
They disagree about food.

29
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.396
Your turn. Say: Disagree.

30
00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.014
Disagree.

31
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:32.832
Distractor.

32
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:36.641
Distractor means a wrong answer that is mentioned.

33
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.215
One option is a distractor.

34
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:42.515
Your turn. Say: Distractor.

35
00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:46.426
Distractor.

36
00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:48.393
Change of mind.

37
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:51.929
Change of mind means deciding something different.

38
00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:54.145
He had a change of mind.

39
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.716
Your turn. Say: Change of mind.

40
00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:01.754
Change of mind.

41
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:03.622
Final answer.

42
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:08.567
Final answer means the answer that is correct after changes.

43
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:10.986
Listen for the final answer.

44
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:14.398
Your turn. Say: Final answer.

45
00:02:17.233 --> 00:02:18.420
Final answer.

46
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:22.814
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.346
Visal, what makes B1 Listening difficult?

48
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:36.407
Speakers often mention all the options, but only one is correct. They may change their mind, so you must wait for the final answer.

49
00:02:37.517 --> 00:02:38.889
How can I prepare?

50
00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:47.930
Read the questions before listening and underline key words. Think about the situation, who is speaking and what they want to say.

51
00:02:49.017 --> 00:02:50.680
What about the second listening?

52
00:02:51.783 --> 00:02:59.289
You hear each recording twice. During the first listening choose an answer, and during the second check it and fill any gaps.

53
00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:01.760
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:02.617 --> 00:03:06.416
Grammar focus: Strategy: wait for the final answer.

55
00:03:06.716 --> 00:03:07.868
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:12.057
First she says Friday, but then she says Saturday is better.

57
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.587
The speaker mentions all options, but only one is the final answer.

58
00:03:17.533 --> 00:03:22.041
Read before you listen, wait for the final answer and use the second listening to check.

59
00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:26.515
Be careful! Don't say: I choose the first option I hear.

60
00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.652
Say: I wait for the final answer.

61
00:03:30.952 --> 00:03:32.197
Listen to the end.

62
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.455
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.523
Changing Plans.

64
00:03:37.823 --> 00:03:39.498
Two friends plan a day out.

65
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.452
One suggests Friday, but the other cannot come.

66
00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:47.407
Then they talk about Saturday and agree that it is better.

67
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.841
They also discuss the cinema and the park.

68
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:53.868
They finally decide to go to the park.

69
00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:59.177
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:01.738
You hear each recording blank.

71
00:04:02.038 --> 00:04:05.389
A, twice. B, once. C, never.

72
00:04:08.933 --> 00:04:10.736
The answer is A: twice.

73
00:04:11.883 --> 00:04:13.778
Speakers sometimes blank.

74
00:04:14.078 --> 00:04:19.137
A, only whisper. B, change their mind. C, never speak.

75
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.234
The answer is B: change their mind.

76
00:04:26.383 --> 00:04:28.209
The friends finally choose blank.

77
00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:34.217
A, Friday and the cinema. B, Sunday and home. C, Saturday and the park.

78
00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:40.242
The answer is C: Saturday and the park.

79
00:04:41.383 --> 00:04:42.953
A distractor is blank.

80
00:04:43.253 --> 00:04:47.894
A, a wrong option that is mentioned. B, the answer. C, a title.

81
00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:54.768
The answer is A: a wrong option that is mentioned.

82
00:04:55.917 --> 00:04:57.614
Before listening, you should blank.

83
00:04:57.914 --> 00:05:02.206
A, sleep. B, read the questions. C, close the paper.

84
00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:08.242
The answer is B: read the questions.

85
00:05:09.433 --> 00:05:12.736
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:15.641
How do you avoid mistakes in Listening?

87
00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.974
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.274 --> 00:05:40.852
I read the questions before I listen and underline key words. I wait until the speaker gives the final answer because people often change their mind. On the second listening I check my answers.

89
00:05:41.152 --> 00:05:42.850
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:49.351
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: wait for the final answer.

91
00:05:49.651 --> 00:05:53.929
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

92
00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:56.754
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

93
00:05:57.054 --> 00:06:00.507
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

